{"abstract":"Generative AI challenges established notions of authorship in contemporary art, yet little attention has been paid to how technical aspects of AI systems are disclosed in exhibition contexts. This paper presents a qualitative analysis of 23 AI-mediated artworks, with a focused discussion of 13 cases selected to illustrate distinct disclosure practices. We examine how model architectures, data provenance, interaction modalities, and energy consumption are framed or omitted in attribution materials. Our analysis reveals recurring asymmetries: model architectures are frequently named but rarely explained, data are disclosed selectively, and energy use is systematically absent. Instead of framing technical disclosure as an obligation, we approach it as a designed practice shaped by the artist. Three disclosure strategies emerge: extended technical framing, symbolic technical naming, and strategic opacity. In a climate of growing skepticism toward AI-generated outputs, technical attribution is not neutral reporting, but an active site where legitimacy and authorship are constructed.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Vitasovic, Leo","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-884835"],"filters":{"added":"2026-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["AI art","Generative AI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing attribution technical disclosure in ai mediated art","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3802974.3809458","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work is funded by the European Union within the Horizon Europe research and innovation programme under grant agreement No. 101136006 – XTREME project, coordinated by S.S. Brandt/IT University of Copenhagen, Denmark. Views and opinions expressed are however those of the authors only and do not necessarily reflect those of the European Union. European Union can not be held responsible for them."],"id":"S01-000.00-884835","ids":["itu-32231cb4-bfb8-4306-b8af-768ab36b4c93"],"keyword":["AI Art","Art Attribution","Generative AI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-28003D50437225F100F866D6AA31A81E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3802974.3809458","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"41da2096-dc8b-44c2-93ad-6473e220f85e","name":"Starostka, Justyna","orcid":"0000-0002-8087-3981","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leo","key":"vitasovicpau","last":"Vitasovic","locid":"b36939ee-d7f6-4e4d-aebf-ff5d0ea2524a","name":"Vitasovic, Leo","orcid":"0000-0002-9919-6191","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid