{"abstract":"Transformation of the urban context is a continuous process of change, in which different interests and forms of rationality are converging. It is often the ground for agonistic forces that negotiate their values, projects and future views. (Concilio & Tosoni, 2018; Mouffe, 2000). However, in relevant innovation processes, such as urban or large scale projects, a design approach is crucial, as it helps to stay on course towards the ultimate purpose of the whole innovation process. In many urban innovation processes however, this approach is often overshadowed by considerations related to administrative or operative issues. This paper is based on the experience in an ongoing EU project, Climaborough, which is promoting a number of innovative initiatives in 12 European pilot cities in a Net Zero perspective. The first learning from this project highlights the designer’s role in foregrounding the value of design in an innovative project. It does so by defining a design-based innovation process to promote initiatives for urban innovation. The paper will describe the three phases of the process: challenge definition, innovative procurement process and experimental sandbox and propose reflections on how the knowledge coming from those phases can be distilled, replicated and reused.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Morelli, Nicola","Colclough, Graham","Neuhoff, Rike","Simeone, Luca","Starostka, Justyna","Zohar, Hadas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808924"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-17","place":"Budapest, hu","start":"2024-05-15","title":"P/References of Design","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Urban DNA"],"keyword":["Design facilitation","Net zero","Procurement process","Sandbox","Urban innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bridging by design a designerly approach for cities to support innovation processes in the urban context","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/files/756101185/Bridging_by_design.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808924","ids":["itu-b6a85780-8173-4d32-b9ee-1f47a10f784e"],"keyword":["Design facilitation","Net Zero","Procurement process,","Sandbox","Urban Innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-22641DCB19593608291374B9292B4C8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/files/756101185/Bridging_by_design.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"urban dna","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Urban DNA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"morellipau","last":"Morelli","name":"Morelli, Nicola","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graham","key":"colcloughpau","last":"Colclough","name":"Colclough, Graham","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rike","key":"neuhoffpau","last":"Neuhoff","name":"Neuhoff, Rike","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"simeonepau","last":"Simeone","name":"Simeone, Luca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"41da2096-dc8b-44c2-93ad-6473e220f85e","name":"Starostka, Justyna","orcid":"0000-0002-8087-3981","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hadas","key":"zoharpau","last":"Zohar","name":"Zohar, Hadas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789527549025"],"status":"p","title":"P/References of Design, Cumulus Conference Proceedings Budapest 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b6a85780-8173-4d32-b9ee-1f47a10f784e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bridging by Design. A Designerly Approach for Cities to Support Innovation Processes in the Urban Context","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808924","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"As urban policy and governance challenges become increasingly complex, interdisciplinary approaches and participatory methodologies are essential. The evolving role of design affects the way it is practiced in these contexts. Instead of solely providing solutions, designers are now expected to connect, navigate, and facilitate collaboration between stakeholders from different public sector organizations. This paper aims to explore how multi-organizational design facilitation can contribute to addressing complex urban challenges, fostering and accelerating adoption of sustainable solutions. We delve into three concepts that underpin the creative facilitation process: the design mindset, futures thinking and experimental attitude. The context of this study is a big European project in which 12 cities collaborate and experiment, aiming to solve specific urban challenges. The paper argues for design facilitation to bridge gaps between diverse stakeholders, encourage co-creation, and facilitate the development of innovative solutions across various parties.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Neuhoff, Rike","Morelli, Nicola","Simeone, Luca"],"cuid":["S02-086.40-755760"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Boston, us","start":"2024-06-23","title":"The Design Research Society Conference","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cities","Design","Design facilitation","Facilitation","Sustainable transition","Sustainable transitions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design facilitation navigating complexity for collaborative solutions to urban sustainability challenges","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"